{
  "id": "12_volt___maximum_wire_length_vs__current",
  "title": "12 Volt - Maximum Wire Length vs. Current",
  "description": "Maximum wire length calculator for 12 volt copper conductor systems. Calculate the maximum length of copper wires based on current, cross-sectional area, and acceptable voltage drop for typical electrical circuits and automotive applications.",
  "type": "calculator-table",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Maximum Wire Length Calculator\n\nThis calculator determines the maximum length of copper wires for 12 volt systems based on current, wire cross-sectional area, and voltage drop constraints.\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- For typical electrical circuits with two wires (back and forth), the calculated length is the total wire length. The maximum distance between source and equipment is **half** the calculated distance.\n- In automotive applications where equipment is grounded to the chassis, the maximum distance **equals** the calculated length.\n- Formula: L = U / (R × I), where U is voltage drop, R is resistance per meter, and I is current."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "voltage",
          "label": "Voltage",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 12,
          "unit": "volts"
        },
        {
          "id": "current",
          "label": "Current",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 10,
          "unit": "amps"
        },
        {
          "id": "cross_section",
          "label": "Cross Sectional Area",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 6,
          "unit": "mm²"
        },
        {
          "id": "voltage_drop_percent",
          "label": "Voltage Drop",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 2,
          "unit": "%"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "voltage_drop_volts",
          "label": "Voltage Drop",
          "formula": "inputs.voltage * inputs.voltage_drop_percent / 100",
          "unit": "volts",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "resistance_per_meter",
          "label": "Resistance per Meter (Copper)",
          "formula": "0.01754 / inputs.cross_section",
          "unit": "ohm/m",
          "format": "scientific"
        },
        {
          "id": "max_length_meters",
          "label": "Maximum Wire Length (Total)",
          "formula": "inputs.voltage * (inputs.voltage_drop_percent / 100) / (0.01754 / inputs.cross_section * inputs.current)",
          "unit": "meters",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "max_length_feet",
          "label": "Maximum Wire Length (Total)",
          "formula": "inputs.voltage * (inputs.voltage_drop_percent / 100) / (0.01754 / inputs.cross_section * inputs.current) * 3.28084",
          "unit": "feet",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "max_distance_meters",
          "label": "Maximum Distance (Single Direction)",
          "formula": "inputs.voltage * (inputs.voltage_drop_percent / 100) / (0.01754 / inputs.cross_section * inputs.current) / 2",
          "unit": "meters",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "max_distance_feet",
          "label": "Maximum Distance (Single Direction)",
          "formula": "inputs.voltage * (inputs.voltage_drop_percent / 100) / (0.01754 / inputs.cross_section * inputs.current) / 2 * 3.28084",
          "unit": "feet",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
