    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Reference Information\n\n**Copper Resistivity Data:**\n- Resistivity of copper at 20°C: 0.01754 ohm·mm²/m\n\n**Wire Gauge Reference:**\n- #2 (33.6 mm²)\n- #4 (26.7 mm²)\n- #6 (13.3 mm²)\n- #8 (8.37 mm²)\n- #10 (5.26 mm²)\n\n**Scaling Factors:**\n- Double the distance if 4% voltage drop is acceptable\n- Multiply distance by 2 for 24 volt systems\n- Multiply distance by 4 for 48 volt systems\n\n**Example:**\nFor a 50W light bulb at 12V: I = P/U = 50W/12V = 4.2A. With #10 wire (5.26 mm²) at 2% voltage drop, maximum wire length is approximately 8m total (4m single direction)."
